//? Title: Auxiliary-Classifier GAN: Conditions, Targets and a Weak Generator
//? Subtitle: Image-only discrimination, explicit alternating Adam and fixed final-epoch evaluation
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A compact MNIST generator concatenates 16 Gaussian coordinates and a requested digit class;
an image-only discriminator predicts real/fake source and ten auxiliary classes. Two native
parameter stores and independent Adam states perform 96 D-then-G steps each, with G recomputed
through the updated D. All 1,000 fitting images appear once per epoch; the final third epoch
is fixed in advance. Held-out source accuracies reach 100% for both real and fake, while real
auxiliary accuracy is 39% and requested-class accuracy on generated images is 18.5%.
The generator remains mostly grey: mean intensity .4994 and coarse pixel MMD² .11795,
compared with .000136 for a repeated fitting-mean image. These game diagnostics do not
establish image quality. Checkpoints, isolated source/class generator gradients, same-noise
class controls and all original outputs remain reproducible in the complete editable program.
)
\toc

> A class chooses what G attempts; D still receives only an image

The requested class is concatenated with noise at G's input. D has one shared representation
and two heads: a raw real/fake logit and ten class logits. It receives no label, target or
noise vector. During fitting, real digit labels supply supervised targets and also choose
the generated examples' requested classes. Both real and generated class losses train D;
only the generated class loss accompanies G's non-saturating source objective.

This is a compact dense teaching variant of
[Odena, Olah and Shlens's auxiliary-classifier GAN](https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.09585),
not a reproduction of its convolutional high-resolution benchmark. The source generator
objective uses the [non-saturating GAN variant](https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.2661).

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/acgan_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
