> Stable source losses and a hand-checkable gradient

For a raw source logit s, positive means real and σ(s)=1/(1+exp(-s)). Write
sp(s)=log(1+exp(s)), evaluated by the native stable softplus. Separate pool means give

\[
 L_D^{source}=\operatorname{mean}sp(-s_r)+\operatorname{mean}sp(s_f),\qquad
 L_G^{source}=\operatorname{mean}sp(-s_f).
\]

At zero logits, the two D terms total 2log2 and G gives log2. For one fake example,
∂L_G/∂s_f=σ(s_f)-1: at s_f=-80 it remains approximately-1, so confident rejection
does not saturate the generator's source gradient. For real examples,
∂sp(-s_r)/∂s_r=-σ(-s_r). Keep sp(-s_r) intact: replacing it numerically by
sp(s_r)-s_r can cancel a small positive-logit derivative in Float32.
The native objective accepts unequal positive real/fake pool sizes, averaging each pool
separately; this experiment uses matching sizes because the class targets are paired.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/acgan_source_losses.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::vector<double> x, real, fake, g;
  for (int k = -80; k <= 80; ++k) {
    x.push_back(k / 10.);
    const auto r = n::full({1, 1}, k / 10., n::DType::Float64),
               f = n::full({1, 1}, k / 10., n::DType::Float64);
    const auto o = n::models::LogisticGanObjectives(r, f);
    real.push_back(n::softplus(-r).item());
    fake.push_back(n::softplus(f).item());
    g.push_back(o.generator.item());
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.lines(x, real, "D real / G fake-as-real", {37, 99, 235}, 2.)
      .lines(x, fake, "D fake", {220, 38, 38}, 2.)
      .x_label("Raw source logit")
      .y_label("Per-example loss")
      .title("Opposing source targets use stable softplus")
      .save_svg("build/acgan_source_losses.svg");
  const auto zero = n::models::LogisticGanObjectives(n::zeros({1, 1}), n::zeros({1, 1}));
  std::print("At zero: D={:.9f}, G={:.9f}.\n", zero.discriminator.item(), zero.generator.item());
}
```
