> Auxiliary class loss supplies a second generator path

With class logits a and one-hot target y, CE(a,y)=-Σ_c y_c log softmax(a)_c.
Its logit derivative is softmax(a)-y, divided by batch size after averaging.
For two rows and three uniform logits, CE=log3; a target coordinate has derivative -1/3
and each other coordinate +1/6. The full objectives use unit auxiliary weights:

\[
 L_D=L_D^{source}+(CE_{real}+CE_{fake}),\qquad
 L_G=L_G^{source}+CE_{fake}.
\]

Both generator terms backpropagate through D and G. Choosing only G's parameters for
its optimizer freezes D's writes, while retaining D's mathematical input derivative.
The first fitting minibatch saves the isolated source and class G derivatives and checks
their sum against the full G derivative. Labels are discrete and have no gradient path.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/acgan_toy_class.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n   = dm::nn;
  auto logits   = n::zeros({2, 3}, n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_();
  auto labels   = n::tensor({0., 2.}, {2}, n::DType::Int32);
  auto loss     = n::models::AuxiliaryClassLoss(logits, labels);
  auto gradient = n::grad(loss, {logits})[0];
  std::print("CE={:.9f}; mean-loss logit derivatives: {}.\n", loss.item(), gradient.values_str());
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.points(
       {0, 1, 2},
       n::select(gradient, 0, 0).to_vector<double>(),
       "Row0: target class0",
       {37, 99, 235},
       5.)
      .points(
          {.07, 1.07, 2.07},
          n::select(gradient, 0, 1).to_vector<double>(),
          "Row1: target class2",
          {220, 38, 38},
          5.)
      .x_label("Auxiliary class coordinate; red offset for visibility")
      .y_label("Derivative of batch-mean CE")
      .title("Uniform three-class predictions: target down, alternatives up")
      .save_svg("build/acgan_toy_class.svg");
}
```
