> Data provenance and architecture are fixed before fitting

The native mnist-assets preparation produces the original balanced saliency pools:
1,000 fitting images, 200 validation images and 200 official-test images, with100/20/20
examples per digit class. Source IDs and original pixels are unique across pools.
Pixels enter as Int32 bytes and are normalized by Float32 byte/255 arithmetic.
Validation diagnostics never select an epoch: final epoch 3 is fixed in advance.
An initial test forward is archived before fitting solely as an initial control.
The fixed schedule is already chosen; test outcomes never select updates, epochs,
hyperparameters or checkpoint weights. The final held-out diagnostics are computed
from the restored epoch3 checkpoint.

| Component | Geometry and creation order | Leaves | Scalars |
|---|---|---:|---:|
| G | concat(z16,onehot10) → tanh32 → sigmoid784; hidden then output W,b |4|26736|
| D | image784 → tanh32 → class10 and source1; hidden, CLASS, SOURCE W,b |6|25483|
| Total | Separate initialization seeds5209 and5219 |10|52219|

Class-head creation precedes source-head creation in D's initializer stream, even though
its source head is discussed first. All ten leaves and their names are preserved.
The reusable components also support finite Float32/64 matrices, strides and positive
custom widths; the original experiment remains Float32 with the dimensions above.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/acgan_fitting_examples.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n     = dm::nn;
  const auto root = std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home());
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", root);
  const auto pools = n::models::LoadSaliency(root / "saliency");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::print("| pool | images | each class | source boundary |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n");
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k)
    std::print(
        "| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
        k == 0   ? "fit"
        : k == 1 ? "validation"
                 : "test",
        pools[k].images.size(0),
        pools[k].images.size(0) / 10,
        k == 2 ? "60000..69999" : "0..59999");
  std::vector<std::int64_t> displayed;
  for (int k=0;k<2;++k) for (int c=0;c<10;++c) {
    const auto row=100*c+k;
    if(pools[0].labels.at({row})!=c)throw std::runtime_error("Expected fixed class-major fitting archive");
    displayed.push_back(row);
  }
  n::save_image_grid(n::take_rows(pools[0].images,displayed),"build/acgan_fitting_examples.png",10,0,1,4,220/255.,3);
}
