> Held-out diagnostics expose the failed short run

A source sign threshold of0 yields 100% real and 100% fake accuracy: D easily separates
these two pools. That success does not mean G succeeded. Real auxiliary accuracy is 39%,
and fake requested-class accuracy 18.5%, on 200 held-out rows each. Class balance makes 10%
a useful uniform-guess reference, but these are one-run descriptive fractions, not a
comparison with a trained external classifier or an estimate of sample quality.
Mean generated intensity .4994 accompanies low mean per-pixel variance .001426.
No held-out metric changes the fixed checkpoint or hyperparameters.

