> Same noise across classes distinguishes conditioning from classification

The grid below repeats the same first ten test noise vectors for every class. Rows 0..9
request classes 0..9; columns hold noise fixed. The maximum change against class0 is .06537.
This establishes that G responds to its condition, not that its images depict the requested
digits. Separately, shifting the real CE targets by one modulo10 leaves D's real source
logits and auxiliary predictions bit exact: D is image-only. Negative, out-of-range and
wrong-length label controls are all rejected before one-hot allocation.

