> A coarse MMD diagnostic has a strong blind spot

Each 28x28 image becomes sixteen 7x7 block means divided by 4. Existing native IMQ kernels
average c/(c+||u-v||²) over c=1,4,16. The unbiased two-sample MMD² omits within-pool
diagonals and retains every cross-pool pair; both pools need at least two samples.
There is no new kernel implementation in this conversion. The 16-coordinate descriptor
throws away within-block structure, and its MMD² is not an image-quality score.
An unbiased finite-sample estimate may be negative; it is not a normalized accuracy.

On the200 test rows, generated-image MMD² is.11794877 while the repeated fitting-mean
image gives.0001357794. The latter discards all diversity, so a low value cannot establish
useful generation. The baseline is fitted from the 1,000 fitting images only and repeated 200
times; it never uses test pixels to estimate its mean.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/acgan_mmd.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  const auto pools =
      n::models::LoadSaliency(std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home()) / "saliency");
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/acgan/outputs.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  const auto   mean = n::tile(n::mean(pools[0].images.reshape({1000, 784}), {0}, true), {200, 1});
  const auto   test = n::models::GanCoarsePixels(pools[2].images);
  const double generated =
                   n::models::ImqMmd(test, n::models::GanCoarsePixels(a.at("fake"))).value.item(),
               baseline = n::models::ImqMmd(test, n::models::GanCoarsePixels(mean)).value.item();
  std::print(
      "Coarse MMD² generated={:.12f}; repeated fitting mean={:.12f}.\n", generated, baseline);
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.points({0, 1}, {generated, baseline}, "Coarse IMQ MMD squared", {37, 99, 235}, 6.)
      .x_label("0 generator;1 repeated fitting mean")
      .y_label("Unbiased MMD squared,200 versus200")
      .title("A low coarse discrepancy does not certify image quality")
      .save_svg("build/acgan_mmd.svg");
  n::save_image_grid(
      n::slice_axis(mean, 0, 0, 8).reshape({8, 28, 28, 1}),
      "build/acgan_fit_mean.png",
      8,
      0,
      1,
      4,
      220 / 255.,
      3);
}
```
